ritten form?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Not least because social influence isn't an attack anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T05:27:41-07:00","id":1240398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237380-what-man-was-not-meant-to-know?p=1240264#post1240264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.... 20 dice in social attacks? In written form?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more like a tome of the Cthulhu mythos. It's not trying to convert you so much as you might go insane while reading it.<br /> Of course, then you'd be insane with a book of demonology.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T09:01:34-07:00","id":1240466,"title":"","content":"Personal axiom about the first age: Nothing is ubiquitous. Crystal-housed artificial intelligence? Cool. Provides services to one specific city? Cool. A group of cities with reason to be tied together? Alright. Connected in a pan-Creation network? Now the setting starts to feel a little shrunken. <br /> <br /> Anywhere I want to NOT have I Am is ~the Exception~ to the detriment of both it and I Am.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T09:16:06-07:00","id":1240469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237380-what-man-was-not-meant-to-know#post1237380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* What was/is Zen-Mu like?<br /> * What (besides the Contagion) has the Dowager pulled out of the Well of Udr? Who built that thing, anyway?<br /> * What is the Shining Answer? Has Gaia found it yet?<br /> * What were some of the other Primordial races from the Age of Glories? Do they still exist in the Underworld like the Alaun?<br /> * Does Cemunian's world still exist somewhere out in the Wyld? Are there other renegade Primordials that didn't want to play ball with Theion?<br /> * If you dig deep enough into Creation's soil, what do you find? Beneath the Darkbrood lairs, obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Zen-Mu is decaying fragments of a tunnel-like path. Bits and segments have fallen away from each other, like ox-bow lakes along a winding river. The substance of the remaining parts are the motes of Essence (and each a Least God of sorts) whispering among themselves as they slowly, near-eternally cool and die. Waving like blades of grass, they whisper and sing about the time a Primordial walked this way, creating this path through the nothing and leaving them (the motes) behind. Visitors are a new and interesting topic of conversation, though their memory of anything other than their Primordial is brief. If you interact with them, they'll whisper-sing to you, in a tune older than the rules of music. If you listen carefully you might make out the details of a secret you seek, but you might find out things you didn't want to know. <br /> <br /> Surprises from the Well might include a call-back from the world of a prior game. If you're a compulsive planner and game-idea-scribbler, it might even be a foreshadowing for your next whole game.<br /> <br /> The Shining Answer is that nothing can ever live up to your nostalgia. She hasn't found it, but it's found her. What she thinks she's after is the shadow of the actual answer, and that shadow looks a lot like the nostalgia she's carrying.<br /> <br /> I'm fond of the idea that intelligent races from other Ages might be of entirely different scales of existence. You may have crushed the ruins of their grandest temple, as you walked up a forlorn valley. Or the whole valley may have once been the ramp up the back door of the servant's quarters.<br /> <br /> It probably does. Maybe the Shining Answer is waiting in the mailbox.<br /> <br /> The layers of Creation go down infinitely if you just dig. If you use a Charm to find the bottom, you become the gravitational focal point that snaps it into a globe. This is probably uncomfortable. The deeper you dug first, the bigger the globe's radius. This is also probably uncomfortable for people up top.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T19:25:16-07:00","id":1240685,"title":"","content":"The emphasis on describing <i>The Broken-Winged Crane </i>as a book, I blame entirely on the Scarlet Empress/2E RotSE. The INSTANT the setting said &quot;The Empress penned <i>The Broken-Winged Crane&quot;</i> it lost all its cachet as a dire, cthonic phenomena, and became in essence the <i>Necronomicon</i> for Exalted. It's supposed to be trans-Yozi, not simply a Yozi-prayerbook. The actual game supplement by the same name tries to club that point home, but it was far too late. If you want to get 110% literal, <i>The Broken-Winged Crane</i> is talking about ultra-high Essence Heretic Infernals.<br /> <br /> See how leached that statement is of all things creative? I wish to Heaven the very notion of the Crane being finished had been vetoed, and then the writer in question got his knuckles rapped.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T01:11:57-07:00","id":1240760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237380-what-man-was-not-meant-to-know?p=1237388#post1237388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the problems with Zen-Mu is that it predates strict causality. Like, there is a point in time, in the history of Creation, beyond which time exists as we understand it - <i>cause</i> precedes <i>effect</i>. Things occur in the shadow of what came before.<br /> <br /> Zen-Mu did not work like this. In Zen-Mu, causality could run in loops. One thing could cause a second thing which caused a third thing which caused the first thing. It was 'mythic' time, preceding reality as we understand it.<br /> <br /> Zen-Mu is fundamentally just not going to make any sense to us. In the same regard that all stories with time travel in them inevitably become stories ABOUT time travel, any attempt to plumb the history of Zen-Mu - the nothing-nothing - is going to run in to this problem and come to a hard stop.</div> </div> </div> </div> I just started playing exalted for the first time about 2 years ago so I only have the one entry from the core book mentioning it in Palenquin. That being said the first impression it ever gave me was i guess like Ry'leh. Gods created from before forms were fixed and amalgamations of things never meant to be were born and then discarded by the primordials as the built and destroyed countless versions of creation in their endless quest to not be bored. I would love to be in a game where the portal gets opened and you can go in to see what things a creative person would put in that would be so alien and bizarre. Someplace so before the concepts that defined creation now was. The gods left there imagine the races they were the guardians or watchers of or for. Did they get prayers? Sorry rambling now. Anyway I think its a chtonic place of forgotten horrors, and patiently waiting creatures with a morality far displaced from mortal and exalted thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T01:48:56-07:00","id":1240767,"title":"","content":"I dunno,<br /> I think the Underworld might be a good place for forgotten horrors. Zen-Mu is...well, the lack of causality Kukla cites is going to be a problem. If you want to read more about it, there's an Ink Monkeys that has this whole story of the Primordials getting together, Malfeas becoming their King, etc etc. It's very symbolic, and Shining Answer-y. Starts with Cytherea coming into existence, and ends with the Primordials bailing on Zen-Mu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T02:57:00-07:00","id":1240774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237380-what-man-was-not-meant-to-know?p=1240767#post1240767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno,<br /> I think the Underworld might be a good place for forgotten horrors. Zen-Mu is...well, the lack of causality Kukla cites is going to be a problem. If you want to read more about it, there's an Ink Monkeys that has this whole story of the Primordials getting together, Malfeas becoming their King, etc etc. It's very symbolic, and Shining Answer-y. Starts with Cytherea coming into existence, and ends with the Primordials bailing on Zen-Mu.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's more Kukla's interpretation of Zen-Mu.<br /> I remember earlier in 2nd edition there was an Unshaped Raksha called The Whisperer In the Leaves, that had an Emanation who'd known the Dowager before she became a Deathlord despite the Unshaped itself not coming into existence until considerably later. Lea made a point of saying that this shouldn't be a statement on the wyld's casuality and that you couldn't (for example) go out into raw chaos and find a young Prince Balor still plannning his crusade.<br /> This may not necessarily apply to Zen-Mu, a huge part of the reason why the Wyld needs time to obey casuality is because Exalted PCs aren't supposed to time travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T03:11:09-07:00","id":1240778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>39Steps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237380-what-man-was-not-meant-to-know?p=1239728#post1239728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve always been intrigued by Zen-Mu, too, especially the line about the Primordials \u201cfleeing it in despair.\u201d No mention was made of any sort of super-Primordial that drove them out, or anything, nor is there mention of any sort of tragic loss or injury suffered there. It just seems that the reality built by Primordials, for Primordials, and inhabited only by Primordials was enough to make them absolutely miserable.<br /> <br /> In pondering why that might be, it occurred to me that two dozen-plus super-entities, each of whom was infinitely powerful within its own defining concept, but also infinitely self-absorbed, and utterly incapable of working together, would definitely cock up their first attempt at universe-building. Imagine the Primordials, circled around a cauldron, each one contributing one absolute metaphysical law as an ingredient to a bubbling reality stew, without even the slightest notion of coordination, teamwork, harmony or compromise. Then imagine them having to live in that mess, realizing that existence itself, as crafted by their own hands, was an awful, kludgy, error-ridden ruin that seemed determined to grind you down under the weight of its catastrophically poor design. That might be enough to drive even the Titans away in despair, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you read a certain Dungeons and Dragons based webcomic, that is <i>exactly</i> what happened and caused the entire plot in the first place. It's called<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The Order of the Stick </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T13:02:08-07:00","id":1241001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237380-what-man-was-not-meant-to-know#post1237380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* What were some of the other Primordial races from the Age of Glories? Do they still exist in the Underworld like the Alaun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there were the Uddshua, the last of whom were killed as sacrifices to become ghost-servants of the Eclipse who became the Sovereign In Chains, as mentioned in the chapter of Masters of Jade that talks about the Timeless Order of Manacle and Chain. They \u201carose from the slopes of the Mountain and the Beast Upon It,\u201d so they were definitely a Primordial race, and they are described as having been \u201csorcerous by nature,\u201d as well as being \u201caccomplished Necromancers\u201d in their current ghostly forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T14:07:05-07:00","id":1241014,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> Excellent point. 2E has had some...strange, interpretations of the Wyld. Take for example the &quot;Which Deathlord is right&quot; Storyteller sidebar, concerning the letting in of the Fair Folk during the Great Contagion by FaFL, and EoSD. In the Storyteller Sidebar, the &quot;The Eye of Seven Despairs is right, but he doesn't know the full plot&quot; theory had the Neverborn wanting the Wyld to consume the Underworld, to remove the distinction between life and death, and resurrect the Neverborn into Primordials again.<br /> <br /> If this were even possible, the Deathlords would all be rushing about trying to suborn a Twilight (without Monstrancing them), so they could teach said Twilight how to build a R.I.D to set off at the Mouth of Oblivion. It goes on to explain how the Deathlords have trouble understanding the Neverborn, but the implication was bizarre. Resurrection is supposed to be the same no-no as time-travel.<br /> <br /> One would think every Primordial Race would have SOME representative ghosts somewhere in the Underworld. The Alaun seem like the kind to cling and hold a grudge, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T18:05:24-07:00","id":1241095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>39Steps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237380-what-man-was-not-meant-to-know?p=1241001#post1241001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there were the Uddshua, the last of whom were killed as sacrifices to become ghost-servants of the Eclipse who became the Sovereign In Chains, as mentioned in the chapter of Masters of Jade that talks about the Timeless Order of Manacle and Chain. They \u201carose from the slopes of the Mountain and the Beast Upon It,\u201d so they were definitely a Primordial race, and they are described as having been \u201csorcerous by nature,\u201d as well as being \u201caccomplished Necromancers\u201d in their current ghostly forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mardukth stan here, do we have any more info on them? Appeareances or anyhting?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T21:04:41-07:00","id":1241155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237380-what-man-was-not-meant-to-know?p=1241014#post1241014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&amp;quot;7&amp;quot;]<br /> <br /> If this were even possible, the Deathlords would all be rushing about trying to suborn a Twilight (without Monstrancing them), so they could teach said Twilight how to build a R.I.D to set off at the Mouth of Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>R.I.D.? What's that? Some kind of spell, or artifact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T21:41:34-07:00","id":1241161,"title":"","content":"A R.I.D is a First Age W.M.D. It holds a Proto-Shinmaic-Vortex (a P.S.V) in a stable state, with the capacity to input when the machinery surrounding the P.S.V will rupture it. When that happens, a one-mile radius and everything in it gets turned into Pure Chaos, with the miles surrounding this ground-zero getting turned into Deep Wyld, then Middlemarches, then Bordermarches, and finally wyld-tainted Creation. It's a Wyld-Nuke, in essence. It's the single most powerful man-portable weapon ever created, with the Eye of Autochthon as pretty much the only exception.<br /> <br /> If one were to detonate a R.I.D at the Mouth of Oblivion, one could conceivably (if the Storyteller deemed the Storyteller Sidebar in CoCD: Underworld possible) turn enough of the Underworld into Pure Chaos to perhaps resurrect the Neverborn into their Primordial forms, due to death and life being distinctions Pure Chaos doesn't possess.<br /> <br /> One symptom of Solar Insanity during the Late First Age was that P.S.Vs were being used as simple energy-sources in all sorts of vehicles and such. Without regard to how easily one might accidentally rupture. They rupture naturally, and it actually takes quite a lot to keep one from doing so.<br /> <br /> Edit: Wasn't 2E quite strange <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Double Edit: I have heard the theory that there's one in Lookshy, and that's where the double-fate-seal came from, but with 2E dead, we'll never know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","user":"Wyldwraith","date":". 08-01-2018, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T06:42:31-07:00","id":1241282,"title":"","content":"R.I.D. Where is that? Maybe it's just an unfamiliar acronym I'm familiar with the idea of weaponising a Proto-Shinmaic Vortecies but that's ringing absolutely no bells for me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T08:19:22-07:00","id":1241313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237380-what-man-was-not-meant-to-know?p=1241282#post1241282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">R.I.D. Where is that? Maybe it's just an unfamiliar acronym I'm familiar with the idea of weaponising a Proto-Shinmaic Vortecies but that's ringing absolutely no bells for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. Sounds more like something that caught on back on the old forums, rather than something that appeared in a book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T10:32:35-07:00","id":1241373,"title":"","content":"This does sound vaguely familiar to me, but from a time when I definitely would have read it in a forum somewhere rather than a published book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T19:22:03-07:00","id":1241632,"title":"","content":"<b>Found it! From Hundredfold Facets of Enlightenment:</b><br /> Reality Inversion Detonator (Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) Repair: 5 Even ancient Solars of the First Age with the loftiest of ideals understood that war, or the prospect of war, spurred technological development. So even the wonder-workers who conjured nascent universes out of roiling chaos turned their genius to crude devastation. The reality inversion detonator (RID) not only relies on but enhances the inherent instability of a protoshinmaic vortex (Dreams of the First Age, Book II\u2014Lords of Creation, p. 95) (PSV) to produce a truly monstrous weapon. These precision instruments are calibrated to hold the vortex in a stasis field, extending its maintenance life-time until the weapon is used, at which point it destabilizes the motonic shell of the singularity and rips the raw potentiality out into the world at large. A RID is usually constructed as an unassuming gray box, one side of which folds out to reveal intricate series of mirrors and focusing lenses that channel local geomancy into a stabilizing web around the containment cusps in the center. These cusps are the resting place for the PSV. Once primed by placing a vortex in the device, it extends the stable life of the plasmoid ball from one month to an entire season. The builder usually chooses three command codes, one for maintenance, one for safe disarming and one for detonation. Each must be input in sequence after the previous, so one must know all three to use a RID\u2019s greatest, most terrible function. Entering the maintenance code grants access to the internal machinery while keeping the PSV shielded, allowing the device to continue working safely without exposing technicians to dangerous radiation or temptation. It takes an hour to reset all of the lenses and balances, a simple diceless action for anyone with Craft (Magitech) 4+. This maintenance must be performed once every week; missing one week requires actual repair of the stressed and cracked lenses and overheated starmetal probability wiring. Missing two weeks of maintenance in a row completely dissociates the machinery from the PSV, and the vortex will begin destabilizing normally. With the safe disarm code, the PSV is deliberately but carefully destabilized, allowing the singularity to dissipate as if it had been abandoned during construction. The RID still needs regular weekly maintenance, or else it can no longer maintain containment and the PSV will destabilize dangerously. By inputting the final code and choosing a detonation time up to a week away, the device is set to shear the motonic shell of the singularity in as dangerous a way as possible while focusing the released energies through adamant lenses which, while obliterated in the potentiality-explosion, spread the devastation far and wide. Disarming a RID during countdown requires an extended Wits + Lore roll with a cumulative difficulty of 50, an interval of ten minutes and a normal difficulty of 4 for those familiar with First Age technology or 6+ for anyone else. Upon detonating the RID and everything for miles around evaporates in a maelstrom of Wyld energies, as the device cuts away as much of the vortex\u2019s corona as possible and at the same time compresses what geomancy can be detected around the thing into a feedback loop. Everything within five miles is Shaped into component motes as the local reality buckles and becomes Pure Chaos. For a mile outside this area, everyone and everything is subject to such Wyld energies that they must roll their Willpower + Essence against a difficulty of 5 or they, too, will be annihilated as their surrounding environment transforms into Deep Wyld. Another half mile outside this ring of Deep Wyld the area becomes Middlemarch-strength Wyld and a mile outside that becomes as strong as the Wyld\u2019s Bordermarches. In these last two fringe areas, potential victims are only subject to the normal hazards of the Wyld, but they must make immediate Willpower + Essence rolls to resist mutation as if they had spent the appropriate amount of time in the area to merit regular Wyld mutation. See Exalted, p. 283 and The Compass of Celestial Directions, Vol. II\u2014The Wyld, p. 139 for more on the Wyld and Wyld mutation. As with a normal PSV rupture, each of these Wyld zones reduces its severity by one category every century that passes, leaving behind tainted land<br /> <br /> Edit: I don't think this constitutes canon material. I don't know this Charles Spaulding, but they put a LOT of work into the document this comes from. Further, Operation Wyld Hand DID happen in 2E. The Solars DID possess P.S.Vs, and if they were careless enough to use Wyld-Nukes as easily-acquired, horrific potential consequence-laden Level 6 Hearthstones, it is not at ALL out of the theme of Dreams of the First Age for P.S.Vs to have been weaponized in this way.<br /> <br /> Double Edit: This SHOULD be Artifact 5, if not N/A, however. Creating a P.S.V requires MULTIPLE applications of Lore 7 Shinma-manipulating Charms. Beyond that, a R.I.D is CLEARLY more powerful than a Soul-Breaker Orb, and they're Artifact 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","user":"Wyldwraith","date":". 08-01-2018, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T19:42:28-07:00","id":1241645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237380-what-man-was-not-meant-to-know?p=1241632#post1241632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Found it! From Hundredfold Facets of Enlightenment:</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Hundredfold Facets of Enlightenment was a compilation of homebrew, not canon, although I believe its author does now write for Exalted officially. <br /> I could imagine someone trying the above as a theory, but I certainly don't see it as an official Neverborn or Deathlord tack anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T20:09:48-07:00","id":1241654,"title":"","content":"I think it was intended as a mechanical explanation for how the Solars turned a huge chunk of the North into a Wyld-Zone, killing thirty million people in the process. Beyond that, you could do much, much, MUCH worse than this with Shinmanic Communion, Shinmaic Calibration, time, and inventiveness...and you could make that &quot;worse&quot; last a very long time.<br /> <br /> SHINMAIC COMMUNION Cost: 30m, 2wp; Mins: Lore 7, Essence 7; Type: Simple (One day-long dramatic action) Keywords: Native, Obvious, Shaping Duration: Instant Prerequisites: Wyld Cauldron Technology The concepts which engender the universe fall readily into the grasp of the Solar Exalted. Emptying himself of all thought and desire, the Lawgiver becomes a vessel for the knowledge of the shinma. Entering a trance state, his eyes become unblinking lanterns and his caste mark appears, glowing the same stark white for one full day. During this time, the Solar subtly alters universal principles with the force of his will, to great effect. The character may use Shinmaic Communion to target a landscape he has created with Wyld-Shaping Technique, redefining its relationship with the great cosmic elements known as the shinma. The character gains ten \u2018points\u2019 with which to edit the region in accordance to his will, which may be spent on the following modifications: \u2022 Nirupadhika, the Way, governs spatial relationships. For one point the Solar may enchant the roads in the region such that they prevent travelers moving along them from getting lost, or infallibly lead them to specific places regardless of where they intend to travel. Two points allow the Solar to speed up or slow down travel according to his design; by default, this halves or doubles travel times, though each point invested beyond the initial two raises this by a factor of one. Three points may designate points within the region as impossible to miss, or occlude them so that all efforts to find them suffer an external penalty equal to half the Solar\u2019s Lore. Four points make the region mobile, able to move (Solar\u2019s Lore miles / day). Each additional point spent on mobility doubles the region\u2019s movement rate. Five points doubles the interior size of the region without altering the size of its borders\u2014the region is simply bigger on the inside. Each additional point spent on this aspect increases the region\u2019s size by a factor of one. \u2022 Dharma, the Cup, governs corrosion, ignorance and desire. For one point, staying within the region for at least<br /> one week counts as a scene spent building an Intimacy of hatred toward a particular social group not native to the region. Two points cause each week spent within the region to count as a scene eroding an Intimacy of the Solar\u2019s choice. Three points create a tenor of desire within the region according to the Solar\u2019s definition; all actions which directly reject this desire are taken at a -2 internal penalty, while all actions in pursuit of it enjoy a +1 circumstantial bonus die. Four points produce a regional agenda\u2014the Solar defines an Intimacy, and each time an individual sleeps within the region, this counts as a scene spent building that Intimacy. Five points hide knowledge about a particular thing from those within the region, inflicting an external penalty equal to (Solar\u2019s Lore / 2) on all attempts to uncover information about the thing; alternately, the Solar may ensure that anyone who seeks a certain thing will find it. This thing must exist within the region, be intangible, of limitless supply, and likely to bring the individual significant turmoil in the future. Valid examples, then, might include worldly insight, occult secrets, or love. \u2022 Nirvishesha, the Ring, governs identity. One point raises or lowers the region\u2019s level of Wyld infection by one stage, for example changing a Tainted Land to a stretch of Bordermarches. Two points summon a certain common variety of little god or minor elemental to flock to the region, according to the Solar\u2019s will (consider the differences between a region full of field gods as compared with one full of bloody hands). Three points may create or close a shadowland within the region, with a diameter no greater than one mile. Four points may create an Essence bias within the region with the same range of flavors as demesnes enjoy (the five elements, Solar, Lunar, vitriol, etcetera). Beings matching this Essence bias raise their hourly respiration rate by four motes. Five points may alter the cycle of life and death within the region. This may guarantee that all souls go on to lethe, linger as ghosts, or plunge into Oblivion; or it might create a closed reincarnation loop, where all residents who enter lethe within the region are guaranteed to reincarnate somewhere within its borders. \u2022 Nishkriya, the Sword, governs conflict. For one point, the region takes on a martial tenor\u2014its people slowly become more generally warlike and inclined to the ways of battle. Each season spent within the region acts as a scene of building a positive intimacy of some kind toward conflict into the Policy of all social groups. For two points, the region becomes a magnet for conflict\u2014it will begin to produce natural resources needed or coveted more by the region\u2019s neighbors than by the region itself. For three points, the region becomes a den of brotherly raiders\u2014all military units raised within the region have a Drill one higher than normal, and all individuals enjoy a +2 situational bonus to all attempts to take something from another person or group by force. Four points formidably defends the region against invasion\u2014its animals attack intruding military forces, and<br /> the land itself rises up in protest, causing all movement to be across what is considered difficult terrain, and producing a -1 external penalty to all military activities by invaders. Five points tithed to Nishkriya turns the region into a weapon against hostile forces attempting to move into the Lawgiver\u2019s domain, raining down at least one environmental attack per hour against any invading military unit, of a sort devised by the Solar\u2014avalanches, rains of lightning, supernatural ice storms and localized earthquakes are only the beginning of the woes that may be hurled at unwelcome guests. \u2022 Nirvikalpa, the Staff, is the medium through which communication occurs. One dot makes the region a gathering place for societies, by increasing its yield of timber or making it more fecund farmland. Two dots make the region a magnet for commerce, increasing the amount or value of mineral resources found within. Three dots make the region a point of interaction between its inhabitants and the supernatural world, by seeding the region either with raw materials capable of being refined into the magical materials, or with those materials directly. Four dots makes the region a point of communion between Creation and Heaven, by causing each prayer uttered within the region to count as though it had been spoken from five mouths rather than one. Five dots makes the region a communication network between Creation and itself, drawing dragon lines together to create a three-dot demesne. This value may be raised by one dot per additional point invested. The Solar is not obligated to spend \u2018left-over\u2019 points, if he does not wish to do so. A region may only be affected by one use of Shinmaic Communion at a time; additional uses cancel any existing alterations and overwrite them. Shinmaic Communion\u2019s effects vanish upon the Solar\u2019s death, unless a surcharge of one permanent point of Willpower is paid upon the Charm\u2019s activation. This Charm may be purchased up to (Lore) times. Each purchase after the first grants two additional points to spend on shinmaic alterations.<br /> <br /> <b>--------------------<br /> --------------------</b><br /> <br /> SHINMAIC CALIBRATION Cost: 20m, 1xp; Mins: Lore 7, Essence 7; Type: Simple (One dramatic action) Keywords: Combo-OK, Native, Obvious, Shaping Duration: Instant Prerequisites: Shinmaic Communion Having communed with the foundational elements of the cosmos, the Solars forge miracles. This Charm must be activated in a region the Solar has altered with Shinmaic Communion. The character defines a wondrous aspect or blessing for inclusion within the region. Much like artifact crafting, this Charm is conceptually broad and depends on cooperation between players and Storytellers to design uncanny wonders that later Ages will disbelievingly mythologize and dream of. The parameters of the effect depend on the Shinmaic Communion elements affecting the region this Charm is used in.<br /> \u2022 Nirvikalpa determines the power of the miracle. One point affecting the region permits the Solar to produce works equivalent to mundane effort. Two points may produce uncanny effects equivalent to thaumaturgy. Three points produce wonders equivalent to Terrestrial Circle sorcery. Four points are equivalent to the Celestial Circle, and five points may produce awe-inspiring effects comparable to Solar Circle sorcery. Zero points limits the effects to only the weakest happenstance, the equivalent of mood lighting\u2014effects with no mechanical repercussions at all. \u2022 Nishkriya determines the strategy of the miracle. Each point of Nishkriya invested in the region allows one trigger to be built into the miracle. Examples of potential triggers include \u201centering the region,\u201d \u201cpraying to the Yozis,\u201d \u201csleeping within the region,\u201d \u201cstealing from a merchant,\u201d \u201cmarching under the flag of a foreign power,\u201d or \u201cdisguising one\u2019s identity.\u201d \u2022 Dharma determines who the miracle affects. One point permits only a very limited subset of a population\u2014old men of Varangian descent. Two points allows the miracle to affect a population\u2014Varangians. Three points permits a category of magical beings to be targeted (such as gods, or DragonBlooded). Four points affect all individuals who wish to be affected. Five points allows the miracle to target everyone within the region. Zero points limits the miracle to working upon the environment; it cannot affect people at all. \u2022 Nirvishesha determines how long the miracle persists. One point causes the effect to last unto the third generation (60 years). Two points last unto the seventh generation (140 years). Three points last until the 30th generation (600 years). Four points last unto the 50th generation (1,000 years). Five points create a permanent miracle. Zero points invested in Nirvishesha produces a miracle lasting a single paltry year. \u2022 Nirupadhika determines the scope of the miracle. One point affects all regions the Solar has shaped out of the Wyld within a single Direction. Two points affect all such regions he has shaped within the boundaries of Creation, and any realms of the Faraway which he has visited. Three points affect all of the above, as well as the entirety of Creation. Four points affect all of Creation as well as all directly adjoining realms (the Underworld, Malfeas, Yu-Shan, Autochthonia, the Wyld). Five points are conjectured to affect all of existence\u2014even those conceptual frontiers the Exalted have yet to discover or invent. Zero points invested in Nirupadhika affects only the Shinmaic Communion-marked region in which the Charm is used. For example, a Solar might lay a blessing of protection on a region for seven generations, so that all invading armies are scoured at its borders by enormous pillars of white-hot sunfire and other horrifying manifestations of Adamant Circle destruction. This would require that the region be affected by two points under Nirvishesha, five under Dharma, five under Nirvikalpa, and two under Nishkriya. Or a Solar might attempt to permanently ennoble all the cosmos so that anyone attempting to initiate into the practice of sorcery will receive this tutelage by the world itself. This would require five points of Nirupadhika, five points of Nirvishesha, four points of Dharma, one of Nishkriya, and two points of Nirvikalpa. Crafting a miracle is an extended dramatic action using a dice pool of (Intelligence + Lore) with an interval of one day, a difficulty of (points of Nirupadhika used), and a cumulative difficulty of (total number of points used x 10). Abandoning the effort at any point before completion causes the effect to unravel harmlessly, and the Solar is refunded the xp cost of the Charm. A botch causes the miracle to erupt in some dangerous and unpredictable manner\u2014at best, everyone in the region is likely to have a very interesting day. This Charm\u2019s miracles take effect automatically once crafting is complete, unless the Solar has utilized one or more points of Nirupadhika. In that case the miracle becomes what is known as a shinmaic potentiality or \u201cMiracle Shell,\u201d an Essence-shaped working which exists in potential but does not interface with Creation. Greater arts than Shinmaic Calibration are required to integrate a Miracle Shell into reality\u2014the Salinan Working is likely the most well-known example of such an integration<br /> <br /> Incidentally, it's stuff like this that makes me sad to see the Solars depowered for Third. This is what I think of when I think &quot;Murdered five or six Primordials.&quot; Not &quot;And they did it at Essence 3&quot; without an explanation how that might be possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","user":"Wyldwraith","date":". 08-01-2018, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T22:07:28-07:00","id":1241676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237380-what-man-was-not-meant-to-know?p=1241095#post1241095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mardukth stan here, do we have any more info on them? Appeareances or anyhting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! From the MoJ sidebar on p. 46:<br /> <br /> <i>\u201dThe Uddshua rose from the slopes of the Mountain and the Beast Upon It long before the birth of humanity or the Unconquered Sun. Insular, strange, and sorcerous by nature, they were never a populous race, and suffered mass purges during the War.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> (Narrative about how only a few survived into the First Age as the Eclipse\u2019s enslaved trophies, and those were ritually sacrificed at his funeral to provide him servitors in the Underworld.)<br /> <br /> <i>\u201dThe ghostly Uddshua stand nine feet tall, painfully thin, gray-skinned with flesh like dry, unfinished clay. Their hands are eight-fingered and seven-jointed, jerky, swift, spiderlike and painfully precise; their faces great empty holes in which cilia sometimes flutter. They hide these unsightly bodies beneath dark robes on those occasions they emerge from the Counting House.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c(...)Enslaving human ghosts through their arts is the only pleasure the alien spirits now find in their endless existence.\u201d</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T23:30:26-07:00","id":1241702,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24378\" data-vbnamecard=\"24378\">Wyldwraith</a> and others, would you kindly be willing to spoiler the excerpts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T18:08:56-07:00","id":1242554,"title":"","content":"Sure Count,<br /> Should've realized that text-wall would be a bit meh, sorry. Just got a little carried away. DotFA stuff is a favorite area of mine, and it doesn't become relevant very often anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}